  "observations": [
    "Settled 960x680 and 1024x728 Tools and Workflow layouts keep fixed buttons, header controls and footer within the captured window. No new persistent layout blocker observed.",
    "Reference inputs, explanatory text and References button can be partly clipped at the lower edge of their scrolling panels; these are scrollable content rather than clipped fixed footer controls. Long paths are clipped within edit controls.",
    "Immediate pre-compositor shrink images can retain old large-window geometry and clip right/bottom content. Immediate grow images can show black newly exposed right/bottom bands. These are retained observations, not clean-frame passes.",
    "All reported post-compositor comparison frames matched settled target regions in both paths. First such captured reads begin about 34 to 67 ms after MoveWindow returned, depending on transition; this bounds observations rather than measuring an exact repaint duration.",
    "The separate old-style immediate captures taken after native geometry inspection were visibly settled in the images reviewed."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The full patch report failed later Results checks due to the validator ctypes Keyboard rebinding defect. This visual scope does not turn that attempt into a gate pass.",
    "Automated pixel oracle compares static text and selected buttons; edit interiors, tree, status and nonclient chrome are excluded. All screenshots were also reviewed at full window scale.",
    "Finite hosted Windows 96-DPI samples do not prove zero flicker or exclude changes between captured frames.",
    "Old-archive negative control did not reach sampling on attempt 1; no differential reproduction claim is made by this receipt.",
    "Only resize and fixed Tools/Workflow captures are in this review; updater dialogs and other feature captures are excluded."
